# A typeset is annotation-only vocabulary — `type shape circle square` names a
# union for a parameter to stand in, and no value is ever a `shape`. Writing
# one at a call was three different answers before this: the interpreter and
# the page refused it at run time, and native built a one-field record and
# printed `shape 1`. The compiler can see it, so it says so here and none of
# the three engines gets the chance to disagree.
type circle
  r

type square
  s

type shape circle square

pub play = print "{shape 1}"
